{"url": "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu/prospective-students/financial-support.html", "final_url": "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu/prospective-students/financial-support.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Financial Support: Northwestern University Interdepartmental Neuroscience: Feinberg School of Medicine\nSkip to main content\nThe Graduate School | Feinberg School of Medicine | Northwestern University\nNorthwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine\nNorthwestern University\nInterdepartmental Neuroscience\nNorthwestern University Home\nAbout Us\nAbout Us Overview\nDirector's Message\nMeet Our Team\nFaculty Leadership\nContact Us\nNews\nEvents\nHistory\nGiving\nWhy NUIN?\nWhy NUIN? Overview\nAffiliated Groups\nCommunity Outreach\nNIH Training Programs\nCareer Development Opportunities\nAlumni & Career Outcomes\nOur Values\nProspective Students\nProspective Students Overview\nCurriculum & Requirements\nCurriculum & Requirements Overview\nAcademic Timeline\nLab Rotations\nCoursework\nAdvising\nSeminar Attendance\nIDP\nTeaching\nQualifying Exam\nPACT\nThesis Committee\nThesis Proposal\nAnnual Meetings of the Thesis Committee\nFirst Author Publication\nThesis Defense and Dissertation\nFinancial Support\nHow to Apply\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Students Overview\nCourses\nCourses Overview\nCourse Schedule\nStudent Profiles\nPublications & Awards\nStudent Resources\nFaculty & Research\nFaculty Directory\nFaculty Resources\nFaculty Awards\nSearch\nFeinberg Home > Home >\nProspective Students >\nFinancial Support\nProspective Students\nProspective Students Overview\nCurriculum & Requirements\nFinancial Support\nHow to Apply\nFinancial Support\nAll students are guaranteed stipend, tuition and Northwestern student health insurance (if they opt-in) as long as they remain in good academic standing within the NUIN program. For the first six quarters, NUIN students are supported by Northwestern University fellowships. For the seventh quarter and beyond, students are supported by their research adviser or department, internal or external graduate fellowships (e.g., NRSA, NSF, Northwestern University Presidential Fellowship).\nFor 2025-26 year, the stipend will be $47,748.\nAdditional provisions provided by the NUIN program include:\nA one-time allowance of $1,000 to help offset moving expenses, $1,500 if moving from out of the country.\nA one-time allowance of $2,000 after completion of the thesis proposal (to be used for a research-related expense)\nAll students are eligible for Northwestern University Student Health Insurance, vision, and dental insurance. A subsidy covers the full cost of insurance premiums. International students are required to enroll.\nBack to top\nFollow NUIN on Bluesky\nAbout Us\nWhy NUIN?\nOur Values\nProspective Students\nCurrent Students\nFaculty & Research\nNorthwestern University\nInterdepartmental Neuroscience\n320 E Superior Street\nMorton 1-645\nChicago, IL 60611\nChicago Campus Map\n312-503-4300\n312-503-7345\nEmail Us\nEvanston\nChicago Campus Map\n847-491-5033\nNorthwestern University\nFeinberg School of Medicine\nGiving\nSocial Media Center\nFacebookTwitterLinkedInYouTubeInstagramPodcast\n\u00a9 2026 Northwestern University\nContact Northwestern University\nCareers\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy Statement\nCampus Emergency Information\nUniversity Policies\nReport a Concern", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu/prospective-students/financial-support.html#main-content"], ["The Graduate School", "https://www.tgs.northwestern.edu"], ["Feinberg School of Medicine", "https://www.feinberg.northwestern.edu"], ["Northwestern University", "https://www.northwestern.edu"], ["Northwestern University Interdepartmental Neuroscience", "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu"], ["Northwestern University Home", "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu/index.html"], ["About Us", "https://www.nuin.northwestern.edu/prospective-students/financial-support.html"], ["A